Description: misc/pipesz test: skip when running without root privileges
 Growing the pipe buffer size (F_SETPIPE_SZ) beyond the default capacity
 requires CAP_SYS_RESOURCE, so the pipe-max-size subtest fails when the
 test suite is executed by an unprivileged user (e.g. debuild as a
 regular user). Skip the whole test as non-root, like blkid/topology
 and ipcs/limits already do.
Origin: internal
Upstream-Status: Not-Forwarded
---

Index: deepin-util-linux/tests/ts/misc/pipesz
===================================================================
--- deepin-util-linux.orig/tests/ts/misc/pipesz
+++ deepin-util-linux/tests/ts/misc/pipesz
@@ -18,6 +18,8 @@ TS_DESC="pipesz"
 . "$TS_TOPDIR"/functions.sh
 ts_init "$*"
 
+ts_skip_nonroot
+
 ts_check_test_command "$TS_CMD_PIPESZ"
 ts_check_test_command "$TS_HELPER_SYSINFO"
 
